# notify.conf — where weekly-maintenance-run.sh sends its digest
#
# Copy to ~/.config/macos-security-hardening/notify.conf and edit.
# That path is outside the repo on purpose: a real notification endpoint,
# hostname and topic are part of your topology and should never be committed,
# least of all to a public repo. Without this file the run only logs.

# Full ntfy publish URL including topic, e.g. https://ntfy.example.net/alerts
NTFY_URL="https://ntfy.example.net/alerts"

# Optional: file containing a bearer token for a write-only publisher user.
# Keep it mode 0600. Leave empty for an unauthenticated topic.
NTFY_TOKEN_FILE="$HOME/.config/homelab/ntfy-pub-token"
